* Local, representative models for the ONE-CHANNEL schematic.
* These are NOT vendor-qualified models. No thermal/damage/Ioff guarantee.
*
* BAV99 physical SOT-23 pin order: 1=A1, 2=K2, 3=K1/A2.
.SUBCKT BAV99_PAIR 1 2 3
DLO 1 3 D_BAV99_REP
DHI 3 2 D_BAV99_REP
.ENDS BAV99_PAIR
.MODEL D_BAV99_REP D(Is=2.52n N=1.75 Rs=0.568 Cjo=1.5p Tt=4n Bv=100 Ibv=0.5u)

* Zener: BV/IBV anchor near the datasheet 3.3V / 80mA test point.
* Cjo=500p and Rs=2 are assumed; model does NOT bound all production parts.
.MODEL D_BZX85C3V3_REP D(Is=1n N=1.5 Rs=2 Cjo=500p Bv=3.3 Ibv=80m)

* Behavioral replacement for SN74LVC1G17DBVR.
* Simulation port order: A Y VCC VSS (NOT package pin numbering).
* Package mapping: A=2, Y=4, VCC=5, VSS=3; package pin 1 is NC.
* Illustrative thresholds 2.20V rising / 1.10V falling, fixed for 3.3V VCC.
* Complementary state switches charge/discharge the RC stage symmetrically.
* RC stage gives about 5.5ns 50%-point delay at 3.3V; not a timing spec.
* Input 6pF and output 20ohm are assumed.
* Does not model absolute maximum violations, thermal failure, Ioff,
* power-up/down behavior, worst-case thresholds or real supply current.
.SUBCKT LVC1G17_REP A Y VCC VSS
CIN A VSS 6p
SSTATE VCC Q A VSS SW_LVC_HYST
SRESET Q VSS A VSS SW_LVC_HYST_INV
RDELAY Q QDELAY 1k
CDELAY QDELAY VSS 7.2p
BDRIVE DRIVE VSS V=0.5*(1+tanh((V(QDELAY,VSS)-1.65)/0.1))*V(VCC,VSS)
ROUT DRIVE Y 20
COUT Y VSS 5p
.MODEL SW_LVC_HYST SW(Ron=100 Roff=1G Vt=1.65 Vh=0.55)
.MODEL SW_LVC_HYST_INV SW(Ron=1G Roff=100 Vt=1.65 Vh=0.55)
.ENDS LVC1G17_REP
